FILE D:\作品集\ResearchOS\research-os\execution\v2.4\receipts\W05\W05-99\qualification_failure_b_revision02_independent_review_codex\20261015-current-chat\review.md SHA256 04d5f574f11bf27520862012088cb2ea49f7dc22e7d1dd3e5a2d951b67182b7c BYTES 4818
# B-r2 independent Source/native fixture review

**NEEDS_CHANGES — two reproduced P1 findings.** Candidate `1d3cc504da79df5bf0f69755011738d5adb827b0`, tree `be0c58bc3d0d103434663d53bf4b03d94ad25580`. All nine frozen source hashes match and the worktree remains clean. Exact five revised paths and the whole nine-file integration were reviewed. Actual/formal increments: **0**.

1. **B-r2-F01: retained directory handles do not bind the selected namespace.** With the original guard still open, the final dispatch directory can be renamed and replaced with another private directory. Old/new native IDs differ; the old `guard.Check()` and new file `Check()` both return nil. Write+flush lands only in the replacement directory. Evidence: `B-r2-review-016.stdout.txt`, deterministic `TestIndependentB2GuardNamespaceSwap`. The separate file-handle test passes: competing file write/delete/rename are blocked, and bytes survive write+flush+read. This is an owned local fixture, not a claim of an exercised cross-user production attack. Minimum fix: native directory binding plus regression in `adapters/runtime/qualification_failure_proof_windows.go` and its test.

2. **B-r2-F02: private consumer does not revalidate complete original native evidence.** After a real native loopback first-gate closure, independently changing stdout, stderr, bridge journal or original rejection JSON leaves `validatedQualificationFailureTx` returning a closure. Marker/proof and all DB rows are unchanged. The native reader independently rejects the first three damaged files, but the private consumer only reopens MODEL Host fact and compares already sealed native hash strings. Evidence: `B-r2-review-014.stdout.txt`, four failing raw-file subtests. Minimum fix: fresh protected source reads and complete digest/frame/rejection binding in `internal/domain/runtime_qualification_failure_windows.go` and its test. Invalid raw-file replay is not claimed: the outer closure function already reads native files before replay; the reproduced failure is actual private consumption.

The earlier ordinary-Mu regression is repaired. The complete base-f48 356-line file body remains intact and only registry tests are appended. Fresh command009 runs all three original groups plus both claim-order subtests with the existing frozen local Mu bundle: zero SKIP. Same-process delivery, cancellation UNKNOWN, original receipt recovery and claim ordering assertions remain.

The MODEL binding repair rejects seven independent DB mutations: receipt id, request body, request hash, route, credential revision, key and history sequence. Existing author tests were also rerun freshly, including Host fact tamper, current Owner project-grant deletion and actual Owner revocation. These successes do not close B-r2-F02.

The independent positive closure census covers all **87 non-sqlite application tables** as sorted complete row/value sets. Only the expected nine tables change; exactly five domain versions are added (Artifact, ImpactLink, Run, ProjectState, EventEnvelope) and one upload. Actual completed-marker closure replay changes zero logical rows/values across those 87 tables and repeats no MODEL call. Raw3/ACK2/rejected1 and unknown monetary cost remain truthful; no TOOL effect is created.

Fresh command008 passes the focused domain suite, including the valid first-gate seed and 24 isolated mutations, late suffix, blocked MODEL, heartbeat CAS and 20 transaction fault cuts. The deferred-FK case reaches real COMMIT failure. Fault cases assert the targeted no-partial-closure indicators; a separate 87-table census for every fault was not performed. Native cleanup tests cover nine specific false/zero/empty/mismatch cases, not every missing/null combination. Exact 15-second broker-drain timeout remains **unproven**, separate from blocked MODEL and late suffix.

The native ACL repair correctly rejects unsafe Everyone ACEs on directories/files and handles conservative INHERIT_ONLY/unsupported/generic-right cases; selected-directory replacement remains a blocker. No exhaustive OS race or read-close-error proof is claimed.

All work was limited to read-only frozen Source, owned evidence, isolated D-drive Go caches/temp directories, and fresh controlled loopback/native fixtures. No original root/DB/API/Core/Desktop/provider/Ollama/keys/worker was used. No Source C/D or boot implementation started. Future C must consume the repaired opaque private validation result; this review grants no Source, package, actual or formal acceptance.

Historical 24 author mixed diagnostic groups and old B29/review13 remain separately preserved by Root. Own failed attempts and capture limitations remain in `diagnostic-ledger.json`; failed fixtures were not rewritten into PASS. Detailed coverage and minimal fix paths are in `review.json`.


